+# RUNBOOK — operator procedures (living doc)
+
+## Phase 1 loop additions
+
+- **Launch:** `hive-launch <order-file> [--worker <id>] [--anyway]` checks the order before
+  writing to the spine. A present `## Predictions` section with none of the three scored
+  fields (`Expected effort`, `Expected questions`, `Expected review outcome`) parses is refused;
+  the message names all four protocol labels, including `Named risks` (required but unscored).
+  Correct the order or use `--anyway` for a deliberate exception. An absent section launches
+  and remains a recorded metric; a partial section warns and launches.
+
+- **Close:** `hive-close <task>` emits the durable close first, then scores the task and
+  regenerates this project's `tasks.md` and `tasks.csv`. Scoring and regeneration failures are
+  loud but non-fatal; rerun the recovery command printed by the tool. `--no-score` skips scoring
+  but still regenerates metrics. Add the human review verdict afterward with exactly one of
+  `clean`, `minor rework`, or `rework`, for example:
+  `hive-score <task> --review "<clean|minor rework|rework>" --again`.
+
+## Calibration recovery
+
+Recover the two lost pln calibration data points with:
+
+```sh
+hive-score <task> --project pln-benchmarks --again
+```
+
+If a shared metrics push refuses, reconcile the branch manually (fetch, reconcile, then push);
+the tool does not rebase that shared path unattended.
