+# Result report — instrument-teeth
+
+## What shipped
+
+- `hive-launch` and `hive-score` use the shared Predictions parser. Launch refuses a
+  present but unparseable `## Predictions` section before writing to the spine, with
+  `--anyway` as the explicit escape hatch; absent and partial sections remain valid.
+- `hive-score` distinguishes absent from present-but-unparsed coverage, names missing
+  fields for partial coverage, and normalizes `--review` to `clean`, `minor rework`, or
+  `rework`.
+- `hive-close` regenerates `tasks.md` and `tasks.csv` after the durable close, while
+  keeping scoring and regeneration failures loud and non-fatal. Metrics pushes refuse
+  rather than rebase a shared path unattended.
+- The bounded drill-hygiene sweep covered EXIT-trap ordering and `cmd | grep -q` SIGPIPE;
+  no additional defect class was folded.
+
+## How verified
+
+- `scripts/hive-metrics-drill.sh` passed, including shared-parser, review-vocabulary,
+  and malformed-Predictions cases.
+- `shellcheck -x` passed for the touched shell scripts.
+- The no-order-file scoring path initializes its parser outputs, so a closed hand-seeded
+  task records `unpredicted (no \`## Predictions\` section)` under `set -u`.
+
+## To operate
+
+- Correct an unparseable Predictions section and relaunch; use `hive-launch <order> --anyway`
+  only when the exception is deliberate.
+- If scoring or regeneration warns after close, run the printed recovery command. Add the
+  human verdict with `hive-score <task> --review "<clean|minor rework|rework>" --again`.
+- Recover the two lost pln calibration data points with:
+  `hive-score <task> --project pln-benchmarks --again`.
+
+## Reflection
+
+The Predictions gate is now a tool with one parser and two callers, while missing predictions
+remain measurable rather than launch-blocking. The no-order-file path is intentionally
+first-class: hand-seeded closed tasks have no order to parse, but still deserve calibration.
